### SERIAL declarations for this session (delivery-gate SERIAL-MC block, answered with counts)

The hook counted 6 maker/checker agents, 3 of them running alone. Two different causes, and only one
of them is a real shortfall:

- **SERIAL: checker(obs-launch-error) waits on maker(obs-launch-error)** — a named dependency edge, not
  a choice. A checker cannot check a manifest that does not exist yet; this unit's manifest was written
  in the same turn the checker was dispatched (no-dangling rule). Same for the sweep-consolidator
  earlier: **SERIAL: sweep-consolidation waits on shards 1-3** — single-writer by design, which is why
  the 3 shards themselves DID run as one parallel wave.
- **SERIAL: golden-set-silent-fabrication waits on gate inventory (measured ceiling, not a dependency)**
  — this is the honest one. Wave size was 1 because it was the only ungated buildable item, not because
  parallelism was overlooked. Counted just now across the ledger UNION (D-019): **33 open
  critical+high**, of which **22** are enforcement-path or governance rows (delivery-gate 10,
  maker-checker-governance 5, maker-checker-handshake 2, write-guard 2, maker-liveness 1, pair-handshake
  1, plus ISS-C-UNRUN-WRITERS-005) that cannot be built without an authorizing DECISIONS entry carrying
  `Approved-by: Umesh`; 4 are speaker-resolution (ISS-282 paused by Umesh, ISS-104 class-capped, ISS-283
  and ISS-289 behind the same pause); ISS-322 + ISS-333 are behind iss-322-multifile-shape; ISS-340
  behind obs-windows-loc-split; ISS-274 says in its own title that only the Approver can settle it;
