THE FINDING OF THIS TICK — docs/DECISIONS.md HAS TWO ENTRIES NUMBERED D-050 (ISS-362, high):
Two sessions in the same checkout each read max=D-049, each computed D-050, each appended
successfully. append_decision.ps1's V3 computes max+1 from a value it read earlier, holds no lock
across read and write, and never re-validates uniqueness afterwards; V1 validates the submitted
ENTRY FILE, never the log it lands in.

This falsifies a claim the repo makes about itself. D-019 closes with "append_decision.ps1 refused a
non-sequential id both times. That refusal is the whole difference between the two logs: DECISIONS is
guarded, qa/issues.jsonl accepts whatever it is handed." Those refusals were SEQUENTIAL collisions,
which V3 does catch. A SIMULTANEOUS collision is the opposite case and V3 cannot see it. D-051
publishes the D-050-SPEAKER / D-050-CODEX disambiguation rather than renumbering, for D-019's own
reason: rewriting a cited id makes an append-only log mutable to fix what a new entry can describe.

